# Nutrient Block's draw is for "put into a graveyard from the battlefield" only: Bot2's Prismatic Ending (X = 1, paid with white
# alone, so it exiles a permanent with mana value 1 or less) exiles the Block, which never reaches a graveyard, so Bot1 draws nothing
# (hand stays 5 and the Block is in exile). The destroyed-and-drew case, the sacrifice, is the other scenario.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Nutrient Block
Plains x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Pearl x3
Prismatic Ending
Plains x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Nutrient Block.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#1.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#2.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#3.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Prismatic Ending.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Nutrient Block; X: 1)
Bot1.Pass
[Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
Exile = Nutrient Block
Bot1.Hand.Count = 5
